          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "kakṣa first meant \"a hiding place\" and \"the armpit\", which MW calls the most concealed part of the body; its feminine kakṣā also names a walled enclosure or a private room. MW compares Latin coxa \"hip\", and EtymDB counts it as inherited from Indo-European."
            }
          ]
        },
